\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 21. Acceptance Criteria\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 21.1 Initial Treatment Plan\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given a client admitted on February 26,\uc0\u8232 when the system finds an initial treatment plan signed by both staff and client on February 26,\u8232 then the Initial Treatment Plan status is compliant.\
Given a client admitted on February 26,\uc0\u8232 when the system finds no initial treatment plan or the plan is signed after February 26,\u8232 then the Initial Treatment Plan status is noncompliant.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 21.2 Master Treatment Plan\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given a client admitted on February 26,\uc0\u8232 when the system finds a master treatment plan signed by both therapist and client on March 3,\u8232 then the Master Treatment Plan status is compliant.\
Given a client admitted on February 26,\uc0\u8232 when the master treatment plan is signed more than 30 days after admission,\u8232 then the Master Treatment Plan status is noncompliant.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 21.3 PHP Review Cycle\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given a client currently in PHP,\uc0\u8232 and the last treatment plan review therapist signature date is April 2,\u8232 then the next treatment plan due date is May 2.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 21.4 IOP-5 Review Cycle\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given a client currently in IOP-5,\uc0\u8232 and the last treatment plan review therapist signature date is April 2,\u8232 then the next treatment plan due date is June 1.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 21.5 Level-of-Care Change\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given a client moves from PHP to IOP-5 on March 30,\uc0\u8232 when a treatment plan review is completed on April 2,\u8232 then the system should treat April 2 as the review date after the level-of-care change and calculate the next due date using the IOP-5 60-day rule.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 21.6 Alerts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given a treatment plan due date is 10 days away,\uc0\u8232 then the client appears in Due Soon.\
Given a treatment plan due date is 5 days away,\uc0\u8232 then the client appears in Urgent.\
Given a treatment plan due date is today or earlier,\uc0\u8232 then the client appears in Overdue.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 21.7 Dashboard\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given 60 active clients,\uc0\u8232 when the dashboard loads,\u8232 then it shows counts for compliant, due soon, urgent, overdue, and missing data clients, plus overall compliance percentage.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 21.8 Installation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given a non-technical user on Windows 11 Home,\uc0\u8232 when they run the installer,\u8232 then the app installs, creates shortcuts, configures local storage, starts successfully, and opens in a browser without requiring Docker, Git, Node.js, PostgreSQL, or command-line steps.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 21.9 Uninstall\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given a user uninstalls the app,\uc0\u8232 when the uninstall wizard runs,\u8232 then it removes the app but preserves local clinical data by default and warns before deleting any local app data or encryption keys.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

